WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.980
From New Mexico to New Hampshire with a quick
stop in Nebraska – and don't forget those

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.610
trips to Mexico and Germany. The story of
Breaking Bad and Better Call Saul reaches

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.190
far beyond Albuquerque - and we've got the
whole timeline right here.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:16.080
Although both "Breaking Bad" and "Better Call
Saul" take place much later than this, the

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.680
1980s set up some important events that take
place later. One of the most important things

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.380
that happens during this time is the establishment
of the law firm Hamlin, Hamlin &amp; McGill. At

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.480
this time, it is known simply as Hamlin &amp; McGill
after Chuck McGill and George M. Hamlin. George's

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.790
son Howard has not yet become a partner in
the Albuquerque company.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.380
Meanwhile, in the 1980s, Walter White establishes
Gray Matter Technologies with his friend and

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.270
colleague Elliott Schwartz. The two worked
together in college and set up the company

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:45.460
after completing their thesis. The pair are
later joined by Gretchen, who Walter dates

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.240
for a time. Her family's wealth leads to Walter
feeling inferior, and he breaks off the relationship

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.239
and sells his share in Gray Matter Technologies
for just $5,000. The company goes on to become

00:00:55.239 --> 00:01:00.636
a multi-billion dollar enterprise, and Walt
forever nurses a grudge against Elliot and Gretchen.

00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:07.354
"But little did I understand that they were
artfully maneuvering me into leaving my own creation."

00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:11.829
Around the same time, Gustavo Fring and Max
Arciniega approach the Cartel about forming

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:16.619
a potential partnership. Don Eladio has Max
killed by Hector Salamanca after being angered

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:21.130
by the two up-and-coming drug dealers giving
meth to his men as a way of manipulating Eladio

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:25.799
into meeting them. This is a defining moment
for Gus, who vows to avenge his murdered partner

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:27.185
by any means necessary.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:32.310
Jimmy McGill, later known as Saul Goodman,
starts the 1990s by running a series of scams

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:36.579
with his friend Marco. The two con men operate
in Cicero, but Jimmy is arrested and later

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:41.729
saved by his brother Chuck McGill after facing
possible jail time. Of course, there's a catch:

00:01:41.729 --> 00:01:45.599
Jimmy has to agree to move to Albuquerque
and get a job at Hamlin, Hamlin &amp; McGill.

00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:50.069
"Just tell me what to do. Whatever it is,
I'll do it."

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:53.479
Jimmy leaves for New Mexico with Chuck and
begins working in the mail-room of the law

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:58.139
firm. For most of this time, he is a model
employee and manages to stay out of trouble.

00:01:58.139 --> 00:02:02.920
In 1997, Jimmy passes the bar after studying
in his spare time and applies for a position

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.609
at Hamlin, Hamlin &amp; McGill. Unbeknownst to
Jimmy at the time, Chuck blocks this, and

00:02:07.609 --> 00:02:10.679
Jimmy leaves to pursue a career as a lawyer
on his own.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:16.489
Between 1998 and 2002, Jesse Pinkman attends
J. P. Wynne High School. He is a rather uninterested

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:20.040
student and draws the ire of Walter White
after he fails his chemistry class.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.860
Not long before the start of "Better Call
Saul," Matt Ehrmantraut is murdered by corrupt

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.810
police officers. He had shown a reluctance
to take dirty money and only accepted the

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:33.430
cash after speaking to his father, Mike Ehrmantraut,
a dirty cop himself. Fearing he would turn

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.359
them in, Matt's fellow officers killed him
in an ambush.

00:02:36.359 --> 00:02:40.209
This prompts a furious response from Mike,
who quits the Philadelphia Police Department

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:44.769
and kills the two men responsible for murdering
his son. He immediately leaves for Albuquerque

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:48.840
to be close to his daughter-in-law and granddaughter.
Eventually, Mike starts working as a parking

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.870
lot attendant at the Albuquerque courthouse.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:56.790
By 2001, Chuck McGill begins experiencing
a purportedly unknown electromagnetic hypersensitivity

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:00.770
condition. This seemingly starts after he
and his wife split up and divorce, leading

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:05.140
some to believe it may be a psychological
condition rather than a physical one. Soon

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.069
afterward, Chuck takes an extended sabbatical
from Hamlin, Hamlin &amp; McGill so he can avoid

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:13.128
all electronics, living in a home he has gutted
of wiring and devices.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:17.950
The 1st season of "Better Call Saul" begins
in May 2002, with Jimmy McGill attempting

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:22.079
to represent the Kettlemans when Craig Kettleman
is accused of embezzlement. The lawyer is

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:25.969
tired of being a public defender and wants
to start more lucrative work. His schemes

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:30.280
eventually lead to him meeting Nacho Varga
and Tuco Salamanca, thrusting the character

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.700
into the criminal underworld for the first
time.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.400
Jimmy ultimately discovers that Craig Kettleman
did embezzle millions of dollars and takes

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.640
$30,000 to keep quiet. Around this time, he
also meets Mike Ehrmantraut and begins speaking

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.129
to him regularly, especially when it becomes
clear that Mike is useful as a fixer and private

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:50.379
investigator. After eventually managing to
convince the Kettlemans to accept a plea deal,

00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:53.940
he returns their money and begins to specialize
in elder law.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:57.630
During this time, he discovers that the nursing
home Sandpiper Crossing is overcharging its

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.480
residents and starts canvassing for a class
action lawsuit. The campaign is successful,

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.700
and on the strength of it, he is offered a
position with Davis &amp; Main. However, he doesn't

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.739
last long in the safe and cushy environment
and chooses to get himself fired. Elsewhere,

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:15.040
to help Kim Wexler get back an important bank
client, he breaks into Chuck McGill's house

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.600
and changes paperwork.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.380
Around the same time, Mike begins working
with Nacho to try and get rid of Tuco, which

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.319
brings Hector Salamanca into the fold. Eventually,
it becomes obvious that it would benefit everyone

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:29.410
if Hector is killed, but Mike is stopped by
a mysterious figure when he is about to shoot

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.509
him with a sniper rifle.

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:35.800
In the 3rd season of "Better Call Saul," Gustavo
Fring makes his first appearance. The fast-food

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.720
owner is actually a huge drug distributor
and is planning on becoming the leading force

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.720
north of the border. It's revealed he is the
one who stopped Mike from killing Hector,

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.919
as he has his own plans for the Cartel member.
Seeing exactly how useful Mike can be, Gus

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:52.780
offers to hire him full-time. Meanwhile, Nacho
switches out Hector's medication, and he suffers

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.479
a serious stroke, losing the ability to talk
and move freely.

00:04:56.479 --> 00:05:00.860
Jimmy, who is now operating on his own once
again, is taken to court by Chuck. The older

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.759
brother wants to get Jimmy disbarred for his
crimes but only manages to get him suspended

00:05:04.759 --> 00:05:08.900
as a lawyer by the bar association. However,
during the trial, Jimmy proves that Chuck's

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:13.720
illness is mental and causes a deterioration
in his condition. Later, Jimmy manages to

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.639
get Chuck's malpractice insurance canceled,
leaving Chuck with no opportunity to practice

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:22.560
law even if his condition does improve. Chuck
kills himself at the end of Season 3 by burning

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.240
down his house with a gas lantern.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.050
Gus begins his efforts to take over the drug
business north of the border. With Werner

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.910
Ziegler, he begins constructing a secret meth
lab underneath a laundromat he owns in an

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:36.819
attempt to control the drug trade. He also
pays for a doctor to keep Hector alive, though

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:41.509
he ensures that the Cartel leader won't recover
and will stay in his debilitated condition.

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:45.629
Working with Mike, Gus forces Nacho to act
as a double agent against the Salamancas and

00:05:45.629 --> 00:05:50.360
to get information on Lalo Salamanca when
he arrives in Albuquerque to oversee his family's

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.750
business. Mike and Gus agree to remove Lalo
from the equation so they can continue unchallenged

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.240
and neutralize the Salamancas permanently.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:01.311
On the other hand, Jimmy strikes out on his
own once again and changes his professional name.

00:06:01.311 --> 00:06:05.259
"Wait, wait. Jimmy, Jimmy, what?" "It's all
good, man."

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:09.509
After getting his law license back, he begins
focusing on working directly with criminals

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:14.681
and is soon recruited by Lalo to represent
Krazy-8 and work directly with the Salamancas.

00:06:14.681 --> 00:06:18.150
He later has to help get Lalo out of jail
when he is arrested and travels to the border

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:22.889
to get his $7 million bail money. Ambushed
by unknown assailants, Jimmy is almost killed

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:27.919
until Mike saves his life, and the two make
it back to Albuquerque safely. Season 5 ends

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:31.409
in 2004 with Kim convincing Jimmy that they
need to take down Howard Hamlin.

00:06:32.409 --> 00:06:36.590
Gus' plot to neutralize Lalo culminates in
a daring late night raid on the charming psychopath's

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:41.030
Mexican compound. Nacho sets a fire in the
kitchen as a distraction, then opens the back

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:45.500
gate to a squad of armed mercenaries and takes
off into the night. The mercenaries gun down

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.840
nearly everyone in the compound, but Lalo
is able to escape. Taking advantage of the

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:54.896
fact that everyone thinks he's dead, Lalo
sets out to prove that Gus is working against the cartel.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:59.340
Nacho, meanwhile, becomes the most wanted
man on either side of the border, as the Salamancas

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:03.949
hunt him for betraying Lalo, and Gus cannot
have him captured and interrogated. Mike arranges

00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:07.530
for him to be smuggled back stateside, but
Nacho understands that he's between a rock

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.220
and a hard place. He gets Mike's word that
his father won't be hurt, and allows himself

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.939
to be turned over to the Salamancas. Rather
than fully acquiesce to Gus' plan, Nacho gets

00:07:15.939 --> 00:07:18.789
the last word in before shooting himself in
the head.

00:07:19.789 --> 00:07:23.689
Kim's plan to take down Howard has two goals:
To force a settlement in the Sandpiper Retirement

00:07:23.689 --> 00:07:27.860
Home lawsuit, which would give Jimmy a hefty
windfall thanks to his finders fee, and to

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.919
punish Howard for his general attitude over
the course of the show. What follows is an

00:07:31.919 --> 00:07:36.350
intricate, coordinated plan across summer
2004 to make it appear as if Howard is a drug

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:41.629
addict, using planted bags of powder, disguises,
stolen cars, and staged photographs. Their

00:07:41.629 --> 00:07:45.789
plan works all too well, ruining Howard's
reputation with colleagues like Clifford Main

00:07:45.789 --> 00:07:47.919
and sending him into an emotional tailspin.

00:07:47.919 --> 00:07:52.240
Meanwhile, Lalo Salamanca has spent the weeks
since the raid on his compound traveling the

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.780
world in secret to expose Gus Fring. He knows
that Gus made use of a German engineering

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:01.300
team the year before to build something underneath
an industrial laundromat outside of town.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.770
He knows that Nacho betrayed him on Fring's
orders, and he suspects that Jimmy, who was

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.319
introduced to him by Nacho, knows more than
he let on when the last spoke. The legal world

00:08:09.319 --> 00:08:13.509
and the cartel world mostly existed separate
from each other on "Better Call Saul," but

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:18.440
in the Season 6 episode "Plan and Execution,"
these worlds collide, as both Howard and Lalo

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:22.580
arrive at Jimmy and Kim's condo seeking answers.
Lalo has no patience for Howard's side of

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.789
things, however, and shoots him within seconds.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.160
"Okay, let's talk."

00:08:28.659 --> 00:08:33.130
Lalo sends a traumatized Kim on a mission:
Drive to Gus Fring's house, ring the doorbell,

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:37.220
and gun down whoever answers. This is, of
course, a suicide mission whose intent is

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:41.270
to distract Gus and his men so Lalo can get
inside the laundromat and see what exactly

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:46.700
is going on. However, Gus quickly realizes
Lalo's plan and heads to the laundromat himself,

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:51.390
only for Lalo to get the drop on him. At gunpoint
he forces Gus to take him into the under-construction

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:55.720
super lab, where Gus is able to kill the lights
and reach a gun he had hidden away. The two

00:08:55.720 --> 00:09:00.641
men fire at each other in the dark, but only
Gus' bullet finds its mark; Lalo dies with

00:09:00.641 --> 00:09:02.330
a smile on his face.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.090
That same night, Mike and his crew remove
Howard's body and clean up Jimmy's condo as

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:10.110
if the killing never even happened; Howard
and Lalo are buried together underneath the

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:14.740
super lab floor, never to be found again.
And while Jimmy is more than willing to compartmentalize

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.560
Howard's death and their complicity in it,
Kim is unable to do so. She submits her resignation

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:23.880
from the New Mexico Bar Association and leaves
Jimmy. The harm that they cause others when

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.841
they are together is too great; it can't be
justified by their love for each other. As

00:09:27.841 --> 00:09:33.520
Kim packs boxes, the episode "Fun and Games"
ends with a devastating flash-forward to 2005,

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:37.400
one year later, when we see that without her,
Jimmy has fully embraced the amoral, decadent

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:38.896
lifestyle of Saul Goodman.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:43.740
"Breaking Bad" is set in 2008, with the show
starting as Walter White is diagnosed with

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:47.660
terminal lung cancer at the age of 50. This
prompts the high school chemistry teacher

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:52.140
to go on a ride-along with his brother-in-law,
DEA agent Hank Schrader. That's when he recognizes

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:55.900
his former student Jesse Pinkman, and sees
an opportunity to partner up with his former

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.420
student to cook meth to pay his medical bills
and leave something for his family. He approaches

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:04.450
Jesse, and they both agree to work together
and combine their talents.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:11.039
"Chirality. Mirrored imagery, right? Active,
inactive. Good, bad."

00:10:11.039 --> 00:10:15.470
While things don't exactly go smoothly at
first, Walter and Jesse do manage to successfully

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:19.750
sell meth and soon begin cooking in an old
RV out in the desert. The pair eventually

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:25.080
run into Tuco Salamanca and enter a partnership
with him to distribute the drugs. As the relationship

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.210
worsens, they eventually end up meeting Hector
Salamanca and are set to be killed by Tuco.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:33.864
However, Hank arrives and unknowingly saves
the two rookie cooks and kills Tuco in a shootout.

00:10:34.599 --> 00:10:38.620
With Tuco Salamanca no longer a problem, Walter
and Jesse have an opportunity to expand and

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:42.810
take over the role of distributors. Jesse
teams up with Skinny Pete and Badger to start

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.450
selling the meth themselves, and they see
a good amount of success, at first. Jesse

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:50.580
even develops an undeserved reputation for
being a cold-blooded killer, making it easier

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:54.690
for his gang to collect money from dealers.
Yet changes in their personal circumstances

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.800
make things more difficult for them to continue
cooking meth.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.670
Skyler becomes increasingly suspicious of
Walter and what he is doing in his spare time.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:05.830
When she discovers he has a second phone,
she initially suspects he may be having an

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:09.220
affair. Eventually, she discovers that he
has been lying about getting money from his

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:13.370
former business partners to pay for his medical
bills. Around the same time, Jesse enters

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:17.260
a relationship with Jane Margolis, and they
start using drugs regularly.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:20.880
In need of a lawyer to get Badger off the
hook after a sting operation, Walter and Jesse

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.880
go to Saul Goodman. He is able to help them
get Badger a lighter sentence when he is arrested

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:29.210
and comes up with a plan to make their extra
income seem legitimate. After some discussion,

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:33.867
he puts them into contact with Gustavo Fring,
and the kingpin agrees to buy a shipment of meth.

00:11:34.176 --> 00:11:38.070
Skyler leaves Walt, prompting him to try and
quit the drug business in an attempt to fix

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.880
his marriage. Gus is able to convince him
to work directly for him, giving Walter a

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.940
private underground lab to work in. Jesse
joins Walter a few weeks later, and the pair

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:50.700
continue to cook meth on an industrial scale.
Despite some initial success, the relationship

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:55.260
between Gus, Walter, and Jesse soon falls
apart. A series of decisions leads Gus to

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:58.940
try and cut them out of his business, but
they kill their potential replacement, saving

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:00.580
them for at least a little while.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:04.820
In a moment of triumph, Gus finally succeeds
in getting his revenge on the Cartel. Taking

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:09.140
Mike and Jesse south of the border, he poisons
the leading members of the gang, effectively

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:13.070
removing all competition in the meth trade
and finally accomplishing his revenge. When

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:17.920
he returns to Albuquerque, Gus fires Walt
and warns him to stay away from Jesse. Realizing

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.270
that his life is in danger, Walt tries to
leave town with his family but doesn't have

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:26.525
enough money to pay for everyone. Ultimately,
he resolves to kill Gus as a way of removing the threat.

00:12:26.999 --> 00:12:31.830
Using Gus' hatred of Hector Salamanca against
him, Walt assassinates Gus using a bomb strapped

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:35.730
to the old Cartel member's wheelchair. Along
with Jesse and Mike, Walt takes over what

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:40.780
is left of the meth business and becomes incredibly
successful. They discover Lydia Rodarte-Quayle

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:44.860
and Gus' involvement with Madrigal. After
Walter has Mike and all of his men killed

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:48.510
to protect himself, he works with Lydia to
expand his operations to Europe.

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:52.650
Even though Walter's business is thriving,
Hank discovers that he is the elusive Heisenberg

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:57.030
and starts working to take him down. Ultimately,
Hank and Steven Gomez are killed in a shootout

00:12:57.030 --> 00:13:01.440
with the neo-Nazi group that Walter is working
with. The group takes Jesse hostage and forces

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:05.890
him to continue making meth for them in captivity.
To avoid being arrested, Walter flees to New

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:09.960
Hampshire under a new identity for six months.
With his death imminent from his returning

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:14.330
cancer, Walter goes back to Albuquerque, kills
Lydia and the Nazis, and frees Jesse before

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.315
succumbing to his wounds as police arrive
at the scene.

00:13:17.908 --> 00:13:21.390
Before "El Camino," the last time viewers
see Jesse is when he's speeding away from

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:26.100
the Nazi compound as police close in. The
movie begins almost immediately after this,

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:30.530
with Jesse escaping to Skinny Pete's house.
With the help of Badger and Skinny Pete, he

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.370
manages to safely avoid the police, and he
heads to Todd's old apartment to try and scrape

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:37.850
together enough money to purchase a new identity
from Ed the vacuum salesman.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:42.470
He finds himself $1,800 short of the necessary
amount, and Ed is unwilling to do the deal

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.360
without full payment. Getting the cash together
proves difficult, but Jesse is ultimately

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:50.450
able to get the full amount and then some.
Jesse goes back to Ed and chooses to start

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.450
a new life in Alaska.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:56.390
As part of the "Better Call Saul" series,
each season features a flash-forward, showing

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.630
Jimmy in the present day living under his
new identity of Gene Takovic. Located in Omaha,

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:05.160
he works as a Cinnabon manager and is constantly
nervous about his former life being uncovered

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:09.590
or someone recognizing him. Still, the former
lawyer clearly still feels very attached to

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:12.830
Saul Goodman, watching old commercials on
VHS.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:16.760
Jimmy's secret identity seems to work perfectly,
and his new Social Security number even holds

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:21.730
up when he's taken to hospital after a suspected
heart attack. However, a cab driver recognizes

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:26.011
him and later confronts him at the mall, confirming
that he knows he is really Saul Goodman. Jimmy

00:14:26.011 --> 00:14:29.980
calls Ed to arrange another pickup and then
changes his mind, saying that he will deal

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:30.980
with the issue himself.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.800
Jimmy handles Jeff the cab driver the only
way he knows how to — with a good old-fashioned

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:40.730
con job. Using Jeff's elderly mother Marion
as leverage, Jimmy makes Jeff a proposition,

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:45.290
a one-time introduction to the Saul Goodman-style
criminal life via a heist of luxury goods

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:49.370
from the department store at the mall where
"Gene Takovic" works. The heist goes off almost

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:54.060
perfectly, and the success gives Jimmy a rush
he hasn't felt in months since leaving Albuquerque.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:57.620
After a frustrating phone call to Kim, now
living in Florida, Jimmy finds himself back

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:02.750
in the conman lifestyle, running identity
theft scams with Jeff and Jeff's friend Buddy.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:06.930
Everything is going well for weeks, until
a scam gone wrong lands Jeff in jail. Jimmy

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:10.780
arranges for Marion to post his bail, but
when he arrives to take her to the courthouse,

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.900
she confronts him with Saul Goodman commercials
she found on line.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:22.300
"I typed in 'con man' and 'Albuquerque' and
up you popped, big as day."

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.780
Jimmy flees the house, with the police hot
on his tail.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:30.180
After divorcing Jimmy and leaving New Mexico
in 2005, Kim spends the next several years

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:34.660
building a purposely bland, no-opinion kind
of life in central Florida. When Walter White's

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:40.610
drug empire finally collapses and makes national
news in early 2010, Kim reaches out to Francesca,

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:44.930
Saul's former receptionist, to make sure she's
all right and Jimmy is still alive. When Jimmy

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:49.410
finds out about this in November 2010, he
takes it as a sign to reach out to Kim himself.

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:54.310
That phone call does not go well. Kim, though
glad he is alive, still wants nothing to do

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:58.730
with Jimmy and thinks he should confess everything
and turn himself in. When he petulantly counters

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:03.200
that maybe she should be the one to confess,
Kim does exactly that, traveling back to Albuquerque

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:07.690
with a notarized confession of the events
that led up to Howard's death in 2004. She

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:12.030
delivers one copy to the district attorney's
office and the other to Howard's widow Cheryl,

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.550
but the fact that there isn't any physical
evidence to back up her confession means that

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:19.580
it's unlikely she'll be tried in criminal
court. However, Cheryl implies that there's

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.300
another path she can take to get revenge.

00:16:21.758 --> 00:16:25.709
"I could sue you in civil court. I could take
everything you've got."

00:16:29.701 --> 00:16:33.990
Nevertheless, the act of confession seems
to awaken something in Kim, and when she returns

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:37.220
to Florida she begins volunteering at a local
free legal aid office.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:42.950
After fleeing Marion's home, Omaha police
find Gene hiding in a dumpster. Facing a life

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:47.340
sentence plus 190 years for his many crimes
as a member of the Heisenberg empire, Jimmy

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:51.470
channels Saul Goodman one last time, acting
as his own attorney and claiming that his

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:55.880
work for Walter White was made under duress.
The possibility of a hung jury or mistrial

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:59.490
prompts the lead prosecutor to pitch a plea
deal in which Jimmy would serve less than

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:02.060
eight years at a minimum security prison.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:06.179
At the hearing to finalize the plea deal,
however, Jimmy has one last trick up his sleeve.

00:17:06.179 --> 00:17:09.860
Inspired by Kim's willingness to confess to
Howard's murder and bear the consequences,

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:14.420
he does likewise, admitting to the court his
culpability in Walt's criminal activities,

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:18.640
as well as his own culpability in Chuck's
suicide. That eight year sentence becomes

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:23.730
86 instead, but prison life seems to suit
Jimmy just fine. He bakes bread in the prison

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:27.949
cafeteria as if he were back at Cinnabon,
and he has the respect of his fellow inmates

00:17:27.949 --> 00:17:32.450
and guards, who all call him Saul. Kim visits,
pretending to be his lawyer, and the two share

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:36.690
a forbidden cigarette, one last time, just
as they did in the first episode of the series.

